==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|skyr|lang=non}} from the term ''skjör-ost'' in {{term|w:en:Funen|Fjón|Funen}} in {{term|w:en:Denmark|Denmark}}. The Latin term {{term||[[lac#Latin|lac]] [[concresco#Latin|concretum]]|thick milk}} in [[w:Germania (book)|the book Germania]] by [[w:Tacitus|Tacitus]].

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|skyrs|-}}

# [[#English|skyr]]; a [[yogurt]]-like product made of [[curdled]] [[milk]], [[curd]]s stored up for food; a thick dairy product unique to Icelandic cuisine that can be traced back to the [[Viking]]s

====Derived terms====
* [[berjaskyr]] (blackberries and curds)
* [[hleypa skyr]]
* [[sletta skyrinu]] (to spend beyond one's means)
* [[skyraskur]] (a curd bowl)
* [[skyrbúr]] (a curd bower)
* [[skyrker]] (a curd vessel)
* [[skyrbjúgur]] (scurvy)
* [[skyrsletta]]
* [[þeir sletta skyrinu sem eiga það]]

